Versions of GC:
--serial GC
  --Only one thread is used
  --work is slow
  --GC is expensive
    --all application threads are stopped
    --once GC threads are working
      all application threads stops working

--Parallel GC (default GC)
  --based on number of CPU cores
  --that many threads will be executing
    --so work will be faster

--Concurrent Mark & Sweep GC
  --conccurently GC and application threads are working
  --but not 100% garaunteed
  --no memory compaction

--G1 GC
  --bringa compactoin for concurrent Mark & Sweep GC
  --throught increaes (more requests can be handled)
  --latency decreases(because of less pauses)

